        {
            "block_label": "header",
            "block_content": "UFC 3-340-025 December 2008Change 2,1 September 2014",
            "block_bbox": [
                731,
                147,
                1050,
                233
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "13 (+) using the values of $M_{P}$ and $C M_{p}$ determined in Step 3. Compare the ductility ratio and rotation with the criteria of Section 5-35.",
            "block_bbox": [
                275,
                266,
                1043,
                315
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Step 8.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                336,
                212,
                361
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a.If the deflection criteria for both sidesway and beam mechanisms are satisfied, then the member sizes from Step 5 constitute the results of this preliminary design. These members would then be used in a more rigorous dynamic frame analysis. Several computer programs are available through the repositories listed in Section 5-4.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                274,
                381,
                1040,
                535
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b.If the deflection criterion for a sidesway mechanism is exceeded,then the resistance of all or most of the members should be increased.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                274,
                560,
                1015,
                635
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C.If the deflection criterion for a beam mechanism of the front wall or roof girder is exceeded, then the resistance of the member in question should be increased. The member sizes to be used in a final analysis should be the greater of those determined from Steps 8b and 8c.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                274,
                658,
                1039,
                787
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "number",
            "block_content": "5A-40",
            "block_bbox": [
                568,
                1517,
                630,
                1537
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": null
        }
    ],
